3. Licence granted. Kwaku IT grants you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to
   install and use the Software, for private or professional use, on the computers you use.

4. Restrictions. Unless Kwaku IT agrees in writing or the law allows it, you may not: copy the
   Software beyond what its use requires; distribute, sell, rent or make it available to third
   parties; modify, adapt or create derivative works of it; decompile, disassemble or extract its
   source code; remove or alter the rights notices it contains.

5. Third-party components. The Software embeds third-party libraries and fonts, each under its
   own licence (list and texts in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and in the Software, Settings > About).
   This agreement does not restrict any right those licences grant you on those components.

6. Data and third-party software. The Software reads the music files you choose and, when it is
   installed, a read-only copy of the rekordbox library on your computer. It does not modify those
   files and sends no data over the Internet (see PRIVACY.md). rekordbox is a trademark of
   AlphaTheta Corporation and Camelot a trademark of Mixed In Key LLC; the Software is not
   affiliated with or endorsed by these companies. You are responsible for complying with the
   terms of use of that software.

7. No warranty. The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied, including fitness for a particular purpose or freedom from errors, to the extent
   permitted by law.

8. Liability. To the extent permitted by law, Kwaku IT shall not be liable for any indirect
   damage, data loss or loss of profit arising from the use of, or inability to use, the Software.
   Nothing in this agreement limits the rights mandatory law grants to consumers.

9. Termination. The licence ends automatically if you breach this agreement. You must then stop
   using the Software and delete it.

10. Governing law. This agreement is governed by French law.
